n travels to Chinese border city via newly opened bridge</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b09639fa6b557d7a5b9b41d3044c66db67fccf911f0d94d13533b37a9ac7415</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T07:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-korean-leader-kim-jong-un-travels-to-chinese-border-city-via-newly-opened-bridge/a-79748580--1461c3f06f45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-korean-leader-kim-jong-un-travels-to-chinese-border-city-via-newly-opened-bridge/a-79748580?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">North Korean leader Kim Jong Un travelled to China’s border city of Dandong via a newly opened bridge linking the two countries, where he met a senior Chinese official.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France: Clashes break out as protests go nationwide</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:490190885b2485618a0dec41908dc7b504af1fde4dd371744d386209114b8ef0</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T06:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-protests-more-violence-feared-amid-renewed-demonstrations/live-79748223--43db314a2270.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-clashes-break-out-as-protests-go-nationwide/live-79748223?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police and elite security forces were out in force in French cities as tens of thousands participated in protests on Saturday. The situation turned tense toward the end of protests in several cities, including Paris.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why Russia's arrest of Japanese journalist is the latest sign of deteriorating ties between the countries.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:21d35a5914fe55fa5d9daf4a7993827038c96cfd5bd3316b2dc982a1f2c25b2f</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T05:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-russia-s-arrest-of-japanese-journalist-is-the-latest-sign-of-deteriorating-ties-between-the-coun/a-79742995--e6439f04b25d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-russia-s-arrest-of-japanese-journalist-is-the-latest-sign-of-deteriorating-ties-between-the-countries/a-79742995?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Japan is demanding access to a journalist who was arrested by Russian security services. The Kremlin claims that Japan is using journalists as spies.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Taiwan: Typhoon Champi leaves 1 dead, over 500 injured</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4779dc9e34407fc3f6982d75c06c2a360aff1cb4e89348161b6bfd428a4380e3</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T05:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/taiwan-typhoon-champi-leaves-1-dead-over-500-injured/a-79748221--2c62bf3b9cf4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/taiwan-typhoon-champi-leaves-1-dead-over-500-injured/a-79748221?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After killing one person and causing major disruptions in Taiwan, Typhoon Champi is now headed towards China.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Andhra, Odisha brace for severe storm</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:666610d05ba9b2a63da288c95ee10add734b3e42d4548460778307b8c2554bcf</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:58:31Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T04:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-andhra-odisha-brace-for-severe-storm/live-79748098--28c155f98f4e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-andhra-odisha-brace-for-severe-storm/live-79748098?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The weather department warned that a depression over the Bay of Bengal could escalate into a very severe cyclonic storm before crossing the Andhra Pradesh coast, with winds reaching 140 km/h. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hitler's Eagle's Nest retreat catches fire, police say</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:56b74595395ba459f912bed6155450f542a97deef7163c4823289447dff308e5</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-24T02:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hitler-s-eagle-s-nest-retreat-catches-fire-police-say/a-79747820--4006d6d04b27.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hitler-s-eagle-s-nest-retreat-catches-fire-police-say/a-79747820?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities have arrested a suspect as firemen try to put out the fire in Bavaria, near the Austrian border.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>France to deploy 70,000 police officers ahead of protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:306586e5b5552e65742fadcd87235104a23726b4b6f3096ecbea840c17cfa318</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T22:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-to-deploy-70-000-police-officers-ahead-of-protests/a-79747655--5faa4d329162.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-to-deploy-70-000-police-officers-ahead-of-protests/a-79747655?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With new protests in France planned for this weekend, the authorities pledged to do everything in their power to prevent looting, violence and vandalism.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ebola: Kenya announces second death</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4519dc7f515e2ed3158ab5d22b975001f50f0b0558942138c1843a70fd6104c2</id><updated>2026-10-25T04:57:21Z</updated><published>2026-10-23T21:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ebola-kenya-announces-second-death/a-79747550--9f3288954577.html" type="t